  "notes": [
    "Historical local-runtime transactions prove the predecessor source only.",
    "The pre-redesign source had exact-source Mandates and Authorization deployments on the supported local runtime, plus a finalized mandate with state parity; those deployments are historical after the deployment-size redesign.",
    "The compact candidate retains the public surface, validation branches, commitment preimages, storage values, and state transitions. Deterministic, GLSim, runtime-calldata, adversarial, Gate D, and candidate local tests pass.",
    "The historical pre-redesign local deployment proves the earlier source separately; current-source Bradbury behavioral evidence is recorded in the current live proof artifact and is not conflated with that historical record.",
    "The supported current runtime returned status 302 and Location without following the redirect; this is local runtime provenance only and is not current-candidate deployment evidence.",
    "Two exact/current-source Bradbury Mandates deployment paths were rejected before acceptance with gas limit too high; returned identities 0x6b5c91dbc8ea969d10508790847ecf49bafb895c331d34f4df95e3c5e5a82403 and 0xdfa2ed87220298fccc574bbe747ed52ec006d46e6e62045f51cf4202b4fb608d were not visible via eth_getTransactionByHash, so no Bradbury deployment is claimed.",
    "The exact current-source deployment fingerprint 1e2ae661318e46a762b204f05a94260a1f2d3198dc2846582bdfa1115319d399 was authorized, signed once, and submitted once; the network rejected it before acceptance. The sender nonce remained 1369, proving no accepted deployment transaction.",
    "The redesigned Mandates source was estimated read-only on Bradbury at 16,516,613 gas, below the observed 16,777,216 ceiling, then deployed once and finalized with source parity at 0xd4C0945533C959b094967781815e31ecd0C345F7.",
    "The pre-redesign current Authorization source was preflighted at 31,890,852 gas and rejected before acceptance as gas limit too high; that historical attempt is retained for audit and is not the deployed compact source.",
    "The authorized compact Authorization source 8df817d76ff0ff5abd5adcfdefb97765261a7cce7bc704ffb44c2e1f28c27238 was submitted once at 16,639,954 gas; its outer transaction was mined, but GenVM rejected it as invalid_contract because the compacted source omitted the required blank line after the Depends header. No Authorization address or code was produced.",
    "The corrected predecessor Authorization source restores the required Depends-header blank line, is 19,967 bytes, and has source SHA-256 306e0ab52bb3c4697bbf4e3c42b62b6eda3a878acee9eecd07ce5a0054ca01c1. It passed the pinned local GLSim/adversarial suite, was submitted once after a passing Bradbury estimate, reached FINALIZED with unanimous validator agreement, and matches its historical deployed bytecode.",
    "The current strictly typed Authorization source is 20,022 bytes with source SHA-256 582463cffbe3e0fd55d3154f905a6b5b1cdb1ae3e2c087c08cedfad2d80d405e. It passed GenVM lint and strict Pyright, was submitted once below the Bradbury ceiling, reached FINALIZED with unanimous validator agreement, and matches deployed bytecode at 0x1e55a34a91b227a1fdc27bd7ce675a7f01dc30a2. Existing behavioral receipts remain explicitly bound to the predecessor deployment until current-source behavioral recertification is completed.",
    "The predecessor-source Bradbury live behavior is recorded in docs/CURRENT_SOURCE_BRADBURY_LIVE_PROOF_2026-09-29.json. The evidence covers approval, denial, repair/replacement, expiry recovery, receipt consumption, and negative receipt paths. Its fresh evaluation reached AUTHORIZED and FINALIZED by protocol majority; TIMEOUT, DETERMINISTIC_VIOLATION, and non-uniform result hashes are preserved as dissent/tribunal evidence and are not current-source release evidence.",
    "The local no-redirect runtime probe exposes the redirect response and local effective-origin policy, but Bradbury does not expose an enforceable effective URL/history to this client. That external provenance gate remains false; Bradbury/public production release remains UNRELEASED.",
    "The exact current-source local Gate G graph finalized on chain 61999 with five validators: Mandates 0xaD8B37Eb0263Ea525BEe0767e5e512E320c71656 (0xbc65aa5dd8b0a3079ad17b9481c85ef20f89a9547e626a9b17adc1105aebde07) and Authorization 0x562FA7DD960338B41C456b60564F964F571A1764 (0x3880d77e219dbfbe1527512fe5434bc15d4fc6f048463d344f1bb020516d961d); both have exact source parity, Authorization binds the new Mandates address, each deployment was submitted exactly once, and Gate G is closed without changing the open Gate F/I, effective-origin, fresh-evidence, Gate J, or production boundaries."
  ],
